<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Spring bids lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cash bids for spring wheat were weaker on Tuesday amid slow farm sales and in line with losses in MGE wheat futures, several dealers said.</p>
<p>There was virtually no movement, a Montana merchandiser said. Snow in North Dakota also hampered grain movement, a North Dakota dealer said.</p>
<p>Price action on the Minneapolis exchange caused some confusion, as May futures unexpectedly rose to a session high of $4.00 a bushel, a merchandiser said. He noted that farmers may be waiting for higher prices.</p>
<p>MGE May wheat futures ended off two cents at $3.90-1/2 a bushel.  </p>
